# Pitch channel reversal for the FS-i6 on this airframe.
#
# Measured 2026-10-02 by check_stick_sense.py --capture, with both sticks
# held into their corners (not swept):
#
#   pitch stick fully FORWARD -> ch2 = trim +503 us, i.e. POSITIVE
#   ArduPilot expects forward -> NEGATIVE (nose down -> flies forward)
#   so the stick as delivered would have flown the aircraft BACKWARD
#
# Roll measured CORRECT in the same capture (+490 -> rolls and flies right),
# and that is what rules out a board mounted 180 degrees round -- a rotated
# board reverses BOTH roll and pitch, and is fixed with AHRS_ORIENTATION,
# never by reversing channels.
#
# The APM 2.8 airframe needed exactly the same correction (RC2_REV -1 on
# 3.2.1). The parameter is RC2_REVERSED on 4.x, and it is 0/1, not -1/+1.
#
# Nothing in a parameter dump or a radio calibration can see this: a reversed
# channel and a correct one produce identical PWM ranges, and the aircraft
# self-levels from the IMU either way, so it hovers perfectly. Only the SIGN
# relative to trim separates them.
#
# Fix it here OR in the transmitter's Reverse menu -- never both, or they
# cancel out and you are back where you started.
RC2_REVERSED,1
